Every `go` invocation was refused by this session's execution policy — `gofmt -l`, `go vet ./...`, and `go test ./...` did **not** run, so the new tests are unexecuted and nothing here is compile-checked. I recorded that in `docs/implementation-status.md` rather than treat it as passing. `sensei briefing`/`preflight` were denied the same way, so this change was made without the awareness graph; the scar (`sensei propose`) is still owed once a session can reach it.

